artifacts/report.html:10606: The upstream fix is the Type‑C class teardown series that makes partner/device unlinking conditional and avoids removing the `typec` sysfs link after the USB device kobject has already been removed. The relevant change is in `drivers/usb/typec/class.c`, specifically the `typec_partner_deattach()` / `typec_partner_unlink_device()` path; the fix is not in this 6.17-based tree.
