artifacts/report.html:10568: The important flaw is that `typec_partner_deattach()` unconditionally calls `typec_partner_unlink_device()` whenever it obtains a partner. It does not first establish that the device is still one of the currently linked `usb2_dev`/`usb3_dev` devices, nor does the teardown protocol prevent a later UCSI unregister from trying to remove the same link after USB sysfs teardown.
